CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ call through forwarding-reference callee: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^expecting code as argument$
--
A call whose callee is a reference (static_cast<F&&>(f) / std::forward<F>(f))
must invoke the referand object's operator() ([expr.call], [over.call.object]),
not be mistaken for a function pointer.  The reference-typed callee is now
implicitly dereferenced before the call type-dispatch.
